{
  "id": "bai_choi",
  "name": "Bài chòi (Central Vietnamese card-game singing)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Folk art of Central Vietnam, practised in the central provinces from Quảng Bình to Khánh Hòa and inscribed by UNESCO in 2017. At Lunar New Year players sit in bamboo huts (chòi) holding cards while a male or female caller (Hiệu) draws cards and sings verses hinting at each card's name, accompanied by musicians in the central hut; the singing also grew into a staged bài chòi folk theatre. The đàn nhị card stands in for the đàn cò fiddle and a generic membrane-drum card for the troupe drum.",
  "recipe": "classic late-2010s bài chòi, ballad Poetry. solo with instrumental accompaniment, tonal language syllable tone locked melody. python skin threaded between strings bright lead voice dan nhi, membrane drum pulse resonant acoustic membrane drum. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
